  "notes": "{据|す}える means to place something firmly and securely, both physically and figuratively.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Intransitive pair: {据|す}わる (to be set, to be settled)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{据|す}える: to set ~, to install ~\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {腹|はら}を{据|す}える: to steel oneself, to make up one's mind\n- {目|め}を{据|す}える: to fix one's gaze\n- {腰|こし}を{据|す}える: to settle in, to commit seriously to something\n- {据|す}え{置|お}き: leaving in place; fixed (as in a fixed interest rate)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {置|お}く: to put, to place (more general, everyday)\n- {設置|せっち}する: to install, to set up (formal, institutional)",
